IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-art11-application`
IMPORT `g4-art11-decision`
IMPORT `g4-tests-fixtures`

-- g4-tests-art11-application.l4: tests for Article 11(1) to (3), (8), (10) and (11), whose expected values were decided from the Law's text BEFORE the encoding was run.
-- Where a duty or power is typed by role and act, its test is a #TRACE, because a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT; each #TRACE carries an `-- EXPECT:` line above it and
-- check-traces.py reads it (FULFILLED = discharged or nothing owed; STANDING = the duty or permission is still open; BREACH = a breach, with its reason).
-- A case is named for its facts. The default reading is the reading the encoding takes for every fork; the alternate readings are in g4-tests-forks.l4.

§ `Tests of Article 11(1) to (3), (8), (10), (11)`

§§ `Article 11(1) -- an entity that wishes to have the advantages of registration may apply`

-- The permission is open to an entity that wishes to be registered, and stays open (no time is stated).
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(1) the entity may apply` `a Jersey company that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- The applicant exercises it.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(1) the entity may apply` `a Jersey company that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES `the entity applies` AT 1

-- A foreign entity (Article 2(1)(j)) is an entity, so it may apply.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(1) the entity may apply` `a foreign entity that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- The Jersey NPO body corporate of Article 2(1)(ba) is an entity too.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(1) the entity may apply` `a Jersey NPO body corporate that has applied` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- A body that falls within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1) is not an entity: nothing is permitted.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(1) the entity may apply` `a body of persons that is no entity` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- An entity that does not wish to have the advantages of registration is not within the paragraph.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(1) the entity may apply` `a Jersey company that has applied` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

§§ `Article 11(2) -- what the applicant must include`

-- The duty to provide is open until performed; the Law states no time.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(2) the applicant must provide what Article 11(2) requires` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 90)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(2) the applicant must provide what Article 11(2) requires` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES `the applicant provides what Article 11(2) requires` AT 10

-- The application in which everything is provided and nothing conditional arises includes what Article 11(2) requires.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` `the base application` FALSE

§§§ `Article 11(2)(a) -- information and evidence, as at the application and as proposed once registered`

#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(a)(i) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(a)(i) the requirement is met` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (i) not provided`)
-- "(if different) as proposed once the entity is registered": where the position once registered would differ, the proposal is required as well.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(a)(i) the requirement is met` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (i) differs once registered, no proposal`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(a)(i) the requirement is met` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (i) differs once registered, proposal provided`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(a)(ii) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(a)(ii) the requirement is met` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (ii) not provided`)
-- (iii) "if applicable": required only where the matters of Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n) apply to the applicant.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(a)(iii) the requirement is met` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (iii) applies and is provided`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(a)(iii) the requirement is met` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (iii) applies and is not provided`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(a)(iii) the requirement is met` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (iii) does not apply and is not provided`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (i) not provided`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with particulars` `particulars: (iii) applies and is not provided`) FALSE

§§§ `Article 11(2)(b) to (d) -- the constitution and the two drafts`

#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(b) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(b) the requirement is met` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(c) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(c) the requirement is met` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no draft statement of purposes`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(d) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(d) the requirement is met` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no draft public benefit statement`)
-- Each missing document alone makes the whole application short of Article 11(2); the others are unaffected.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no draft statement of purposes`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no draft public benefit statement`) FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(c) the requirement is met` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)

§§§ `Article 11(2)(e) -- financial details`

-- (i) "the applicant's most recent, if any, financial accounts".
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(i) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(i) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: accounts exist and are not given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(i) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: accounts exist and are given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(i) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: no accounts exist and none are given`)

-- (ii), the second requirement: "if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, a draft of the proposed statement under that Order".
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement of a draft statement is met` `the base application` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement of a draft statement is met` `the base application` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement of a draft statement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a draft statement under the Order is given`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` `the base application` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a draft statement under the Order is given`) TRUE

-- (iii) "any other financial information that would be required if the application were for registration under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008".
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(iii) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(iii) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: the Non-Profit Organizations Law requires more and it is not given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(iii) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: the Non-Profit Organizations Law requires more and it is given`)

-- (iv) "if the applicant is not requesting entry in the restricted section of the register, any further financial information prescribed by the Minister by Order".
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(iv) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(iv) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: an Order prescribes more, the general section is requested, it is not given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(iv) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: an Order prescribes more, the restricted section is requested, it is not given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(iv) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: no Order prescribes more, the general section is requested, none is given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(iv) the requirement is met` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: an Order prescribes more, the general section is requested, it is given`)

§§§ `Article 11(2)(e)(ii) -- payments to governors in the twelve months preceding the application (period P5)`

-- The application is lodged and complete on 15 March 2026. On the default reading the twelve months are 15 March 2025 to 14 March 2026, both inclusive.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` `the default reading` `the base application` EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2025 3 15), (YMD 2026 3 14))
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the base application` (YMD 2025 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the base application` (YMD 2025 3 14)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the base application` (YMD 2026 3 14)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the base application` (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` `the default reading` `the base application` (YMD 2025 12 25)
-- A payment in the period that the application does not disclose leaves the application short of Article 11(2)(e)(ii).
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2025 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2025 made and disclosed`)
-- A payment on the day before the first day, or on the day of the application, is outside the period and need not be disclosed.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 14 March 2025 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2026 made and not disclosed`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 1 March 2026 made and not disclosed`)
-- Two payments, one inside the period and disclosed, one outside and not: the requirement is met.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: two payments made, only the one in the period disclosed`)
-- The whole application: a payment in the period not disclosed makes it short, disclosed makes it complete.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 1 March 2026 made and not disclosed`) FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2025 made and disclosed`) FALSE
-- A payment is disclosed when its details (who, when, how much) are given; the facts about the payee that fork F4.11 reads are not details of the payment.
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2025 made and its details disclosed without the facts about the payee`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` `the default reading` (`the base application with financial details` `financial details: a payment on 15 March 2025 made and disclosed with a different amount`)
-- Which payments the paragraph reaches (payment record by payment record).
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `the default reading` `the base application` `payment of 200 to Anna on 15 March 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` `the default reading` `the base application` `payment of 100 to Anna on 14 March 2025`

§§§ `Article 11(8)(b) -- relief by an Order for a described applicant (applies to paragraph (2))`

-- Without a copy of the constitution the application is short of paragraph (2)(b) ...
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(b) the requirement is met` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)
-- ... unless an Order under Article 11(8)(b)(i) disapplies that provision for this applicant, the other provisions staying.
`the application without a constitution copy, for which the Order disapplies the provision` MEANS `Application for registration` WITH
    dates IS `dates: lodged and complete on 15 March 2026`
    `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS `particulars: everything provided, paragraph (iii) does not apply`
    `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS `documents: no copy of the constitution`
    `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS `financial details: nothing further required`
    `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS `other requirements: none arise`
    `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS LIST `a copy of the applicant's constitution`

`the application without a constitution copy, for which the Order disapplies a different provision` MEANS `Application for registration` WITH
    dates IS `dates: lodged and complete on 15 March 2026`
    `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS `particulars: everything provided, paragraph (iii) does not apply`
    `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS `documents: no copy of the constitution`
    `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS `financial details: nothing further required`
    `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS `other requirements: none arise`
    `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS LIST `a draft of the registered public benefit statement`

#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(b) the requirement is met` `the application without a constitution copy, for which the Order disapplies the provision`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(b) the requirement is met` `the application without a constitution copy, for which the Order disapplies a different provision`
#ASSERT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` `the application without a constitution copy, for which the Order disapplies the provision` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` `the default reading` `the application without a constitution copy, for which the Order disapplies a different provision` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `a copy of the applicant's constitution` `the application without a constitution copy, for which the Order disapplies the provision`
#ASSERT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `a copy of the applicant's constitution` `the base application`

§§§ `Article 11(2)(f) -- other information, documents and evidence`

#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(f)(i) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(f)(i) the requirement is met` (`the base application with other requirements` `other requirements: Regulations require more and it is not given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(f)(i) the requirement is met` (`the base application with other requirements` `other requirements: Regulations require more and it is given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(f)(ii) the requirement is met` `the base application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(2)(f)(ii) the requirement is met` (`the base application with other requirements` `other requirements: the Commissioner has asked for more and it is not given`)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(f)(ii) the requirement is met` (`the base application with other requirements` `other requirements: the Commissioner has asked for more and it is given`)
-- Compliance with the chapeau of Article 11(4) also needs the procedure that Regulations under Article 11(3)(b) prescribe.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4) the applicant has complied with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)` `the default reading` (`the base application with other requirements` `other requirements: the procedure under the Regulations was not followed`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 11(4) the applicant has complied with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)` `the default reading` `the base application` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(4) the applicant has complied with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)` `the default reading` `the base application` FALSE FALSE

§§ `Article 11(3) -- Regulations on information and procedure`

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(3)(a) the States may prescribe other information, documents or evidence` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(3)(a) the States may prescribe other information, documents or evidence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the States` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the States`, `make Regulations prescribing other information, documents or evidence to be provided on an application`) AT 30

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(3)(b) the States may make further provision as to the procedure` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(3)(b) the States may make further provision as to the procedure` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the States` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the States`, `make Regulations making further provision as to the procedure for making an application`) AT 30

§§ `Article 11(8) -- Orders of the Minister`

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Minister may provide for the period within which the Commissioner must decide an application` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Minister may provide for the period within which the Commissioner must decide an application` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `make an Order providing for the period within which the Commissioner must decide an application`) AT 30

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(a)(ii) the Minister may provide for the notification of decisions and of reasons for refusal` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(a)(ii) the Minister may provide for the notification of decisions and of reasons for refusal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `make an Order providing for the notification of decisions and of reasons for refusal`) AT 30

-- (b): "after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities".
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE

-- (b)(i): consulted both, and it appears to the Minister that the description needs relief by virtue of small size or lack of resources or expertise.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(i) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a prescribed description of applicant` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(i) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a prescribed description of applicant` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `make an Order that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a described applicant`) AT 30

-- Without the consultation of the Commissioner, no permission arises.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(i) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a prescribed description of applicant` FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- Without the consultation of the representative body, no permission arises.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(i) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a prescribed description of applicant` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- Without the Minister's appearance that relief is needed, no permission arises.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(i) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a prescribed description of applicant` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- (b)(ii): the same preconditions, with the Minister's appearance that the modification gives reasonable relief.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(ii) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) applies to a prescribed description of applicant subject to a modification` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(ii) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) applies to a prescribed description of applicant subject to a modification` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `make an Order that a provision of Article 11(2) applies to a described applicant subject to a modification`) AT 30

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(ii) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) applies to a prescribed description of applicant subject to a modification` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(8)(b)(ii) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) applies to a prescribed description of applicant subject to a modification` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 365)

§§§ `Article 11(8)(a)(i) -- the period for the Commissioner's decision (periods P6, P7)`

-- The application is lodged on 1 March 2026 and is complete on 20 March 2026; an Order (not among the sources) allows 30 days. On the default reading the period runs from the day lodged, starting the next day.
`the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026` MEANS `the base application with dates` `dates: lodged on 1 March 2026, complete on 20 March 2026`

#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026` (JUST 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026` (JUST 30) (YMD 2026 3 5)
-- No Order is among the sources: without a length the model refuses, by name, and does not say that a decision is late or in time.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026` NOTHING BECAUSE "no Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixing the period for the Commissioner's decision is encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` `the default reading` `the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026` NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 31) BECAUSE "no Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixing the period for the Commissioner's decision is encoded in this model"

§§ `Article 11(10) and (11) -- the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`

-- (10)(a) and (b): the applicant is required to be registered under that Law and is not.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(10)(a) the applicant must provide the additional information with the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(10)(a) the applicant must provide the additional information with the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `provide with the application the additional information that must be provided to the JFSC`) AT 1

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(10)(a) the applicant must provide the additional information with the application` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(10)(b) the applicant must request to be registered under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(10)(b) the applicant must request to be registered under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `request to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`) AT 1

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(10)(b) the applicant must request to be registered under that Law` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- Both duties together: one done leaves the other standing, both done discharges.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(10) the applicant must provide the additional information and request to be registered under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `provide with the application the additional information that must be provided to the JFSC`) AT 1

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(10) the applicant must provide the additional information and request to be registered under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `provide with the application the additional information that must be provided to the JFSC`) AT 1
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `request to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`) AT 2

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(10) the applicant must provide the additional information and request to be registered under that Law` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- (11)(a): the Commissioner passes the request on; (11)(b): the JFSC treats it as an application.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(a) the Commissioner must pass the request to the JFSC` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(a) the Commissioner must pass the request to the JFSC` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `pass the request, with the information and documents, to the JFSC`) AT 3

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(a) the Commissioner must pass the request to the JFSC` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(b) the JFSC must treat the request as an application for registration under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(b) the JFSC must treat the request as an application for registration under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Jersey Financial Services Commission` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Jersey Financial Services Commission`, `treat the request, with the information and documents, as an application for registration under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`) AT 5

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(b) the JFSC must treat the request as an application for registration under that Law` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)
